[ti:Room 101 - I.L.B.B]
[ar:EdgarAllanMusic]
[al:1984s.text - Rectified]
[length:03:15.89]

[00:03.46]You asked me once what was in Room 101. You always knew
[00:07.83]It's different for every man
[00:09.86]For you, Winston, it happens to be rats
[00:20.02]White tiles, endless corridors, the smell of fear
[00:29.35]They break the body but the mind is what they tear
[00:37.75]I scream for mercy, I scream for release
[00:42.68]Until the thing I love most becomes the beast
[00:47.57]The wire cage at my face, and nothing left to keep
[00:52.36]I hear the latch, I hear my voice before I speak
[00:56.77]Do it to Julia! Not me... Julia, not me
[01:07.96]I'll love Big Brother... I'm learning how
[01:12.02]The last piece of me is leaving, I can feel it now
[01:16.31]It's getting sweet and easy, and I'm smiling through it now
[01:21.15]I'll love Big Brother... I'm learning how
[01:36.34]Chestnut Tree Café, the gin tastes of cloves
[01:40.78]I play chess alone where the sunlight goes
[01:45.35]Two and two make five, I draw it in the dust
[01:50.19]Victory in Africa... I sing it because I must
[01:54.92]Under the spreading chestnut tree
[01:58.88]They said I sold you, you sold me, and we both walked free
[02:04.23]March in the park, the wind was thin and cold
[02:08.18]She said, "I betrayed you." I said, "I betrayed you."
[02:13.55]Snakes and ladders, mother laughing, little sister too
[02:18.94]Just a memory that's false... I let it go
[02:24.77]I love Big Brother... I love Big Brother now
[02:28.87]The last piece of me is gone, I don't know how
[02:37.55]And I... love... Big Brother
[02:55.97]And I love Big Brother
[03:02.56]He loved Big Brother
[03:06.15]I do not believe
[03:07.06]That the kind of society I describe
[03:08.92]Necessarily will arrive
[03:11.19]But something resembling it could arrive
[03:14.94]
